1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,753
You'd never guess what made this sound.

2
00:00:01,773 --> 00:00:06,973
[NOAA recording]

3
00:00:07,358 --> 00:00:10,038
Sensors over five thousand kilometers apart heard

4
00:00:10,058 --> 00:00:12,572
it in 1997. What was it, actually?

5
00:00:12,592 --> 00:00:14,405
People wondered about a giant animal.

6
00:00:14,425 --> 00:00:17,682
But in 2008, NOAA tracked a huge iceberg

7
00:00:17,702 --> 00:00:20,533
breaking apart. Its icequakes looked very similar.

8
00:00:20,553 --> 00:00:23,080
The Bloop was ice, cracking. Solved.

9
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,175
Five more ocean sounds are on the channel.
